# `module::Field::objective`

[Back to `module::Field`](../Field.md)

The loss as the number a minimiser should reduce: the same value as `loss_value`.

## Signature

```cpp
double module::Field::objective(const pluss::Series &target_prices, pluss::Config cfg = {}) const;
```

## What It Does

A synonym of [`loss_value`](loss_value.md): the code is shared. It exists so that a fitting program reads naturally, `objective(quotes)` being what a minimiser drives to zero; to feed a minimiser a function of the parameters, use [`bind_objective`](bind_objective.md), which freezes the field and the quotes.

## Parameters

`const pluss::Series &target_prices`
: One quote per option.

`pluss::Config cfg`
: Device.

## Returns

The loss.

## Errors

- As for `loss`.

## Practical Examples

### Example 1

The objective equals the loss value.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace fin = pluss::subsp::math::finance;
namespace mod = fin::module;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(10));
  mod::Field field{.instrument = {.type = fin::pricing::Call, .strike = pluss::series::linspace(80.0, 120.0, 5, pluss::ScalarType::Float64), .maturity = pluss::make_series({1.0})},
                   .market = {.spot = pluss::make_series({100.0}), .rate = pluss::make_series({0.02}), .dividend_yield = pluss::make_series({0.0})},
                   .model = fin::model::make(fin::model::Kind::Heston, {1.5, 0.04, 0.3, -0.7, 0.04}),
                   .controls = {.engine = mod::Engine::Cos, .risk = mod::Risk::PriceOnly}};
  const Series prices = field.price().price;
  const Series quotes = prices + pluss::make_series({0.30, -0.20, 0.10, -0.40, 0.25});

  out.writeln("objective =", field.objective(quotes), ", loss_value =", field.loss_value(quotes));
}
```

### Example 2

A scan of the objective over one parameter shows its shape: a minimum at the parameter that made the quotes.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace fin = pluss::subsp::math::finance;
namespace mod = fin::module;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(10));
  mod::Field field{.instrument = {.type = fin::pricing::Call, .strike = pluss::series::linspace(80.0, 120.0, 5, pluss::ScalarType::Float64), .maturity = pluss::make_series({1.0})},
                   .market = {.spot = pluss::make_series({100.0}), .rate = pluss::make_series({0.02}), .dividend_yield = pluss::make_series({0.0})},
                   .model = fin::model::make(fin::model::Kind::Heston, {1.5, 0.04, 0.3, -0.7, 0.04}),
                   .controls = {.engine = mod::Engine::Cos, .risk = mod::Risk::PriceOnly}};

  const Series quotes = field.price().price;
  for (const double rho : {-0.9, -0.8, -0.7, -0.6, -0.5}) {
    field.model.as<fin::model::Heston>().rho = pluss::make_series({rho});
    out.writeln("rho", rho, ": objective =", field.objective(quotes));
  }
}
```

### Example 3

The Huber loss caps the influence of one wild quote. With a single quote 5.0 away, MSE explodes while Huber grows linearly.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace fin = pluss::subsp::math::finance;
namespace mod = fin::module;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(6));
  mod::Field field{.instrument = {.type = fin::pricing::Call, .strike = pluss::series::linspace(80.0, 120.0, 5, pluss::ScalarType::Float64), .maturity = pluss::make_series({1.0})},
                   .market = {.spot = pluss::make_series({100.0}), .rate = pluss::make_series({0.02}), .dividend_yield = pluss::make_series({0.0})},
                   .model = fin::model::make(fin::model::Kind::Heston, {1.5, 0.04, 0.3, -0.7, 0.04}),
                   .controls = {.engine = mod::Engine::Cos, .risk = mod::Risk::PriceOnly}};

  Series quotes = field.price().price;
  quotes = quotes + pluss::make_series({0.0, 0.0, 5.0, 0.0, 0.0});
  field.controls.loss = mod::Loss::MSE;
  const double mse = field.objective(quotes);
  field.controls.loss = mod::Loss::Huber;
  out.writeln("MSE =", mse, ", Huber(0.05) =", field.objective(quotes));
}
```

